WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.990
The year was 1983, and seven year old Andrea
Bradbury was wandering the streets of Nashville,

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:06.990
Tennessee.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:10.920
One of her favourite activities was to head
down to the local movie theater and fantasize

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.610
about the movies she’d one day be old enough
to see.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:20.250
This fateful weekend, Andrea’s local theater
was playing a brand new release: Jaws 3D.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:25.230
What she didn’t know is that this simple,
innocent activity would bring little Andrea

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:31.550
into dangerous contact with SCP - 178 and
change her life forever.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:36.149
Jaws 3D isn’t exactly a classic - it was
one of the many forgettable sequels pumped

00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:39.450
out to cash in on the 3D craze of the early
1980s.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:44.250
People paid extra for the privilege of sitting
in the dark with an uncomfortable pair of

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:49.140
cardboard glasses while cheesy effects leapt
out of the screen towards them.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.410
Many of the moviegoers simply threw away the
cheap, disposable glasses as soon as they

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:57.730
left the theater, leaving them scattered on
the sidewalk outside.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:01.670
Seeing a pair of 3D glasses on the ground,
right there for the taking, was the highlight

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:03.399
of little Andrea’s week.

00:01:03.399 --> 00:01:07.700
She may not have been old enough to see any
of the movies, but she knew that a local shop

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:13.100
sold books with images that popped off the
page with a simple pair of 3D glasses.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:18.119
Excited by the prospect of getting to experience
3D, Andrea grabbed a pair of glasses and ran

00:01:18.119 --> 00:01:19.970
straight for the bookstore.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:25.070
Later that night, she was in her bedroom,
with a stereoscopic image of a Ferris wheel..

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:30.500
Andrea adjusted the glasses - and the Ferris
wheel really did pop right off the page.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.149
She marveled at the image coming out of the
book and felt like she could almost touch

00:01:34.149 --> 00:01:35.149
it.

00:01:35.149 --> 00:01:38.470
But suddenly a strange feeling came over her.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:42.390
She had the feeling that she wasn’t… alone.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:46.430
Still wearing the glasses, Andrea looked up
from her book and saw it, standing in the

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:48.320
corner of her room.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.380
Something huge.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:51.799
Something monstrous.

00:01:51.799 --> 00:01:56.549
Andrea’s parents heard her scream and came
rushing into her room.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.240
There was their little girl, dead.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:03.750
It looked like she’d been mauled to death
by a wild animal, but there was no sign of

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:04.750
her killer.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:08.800
The windows were shut tight, unable to be
opened from outside.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:13.350
It was like whatever horrible creature had
done this had vanished into thin air.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:17.640
The coroner's report didn’t give any other
clues as to who could have done this, except

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:23.150
that whoever, or whatever had murdered her,
it appeared to have three long and incredibly

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:25.230
sharp claws.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:29.470
The terrible tragedy of Andrea’s death rocked
Nashville, but it never made the national

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:30.470
papers.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:31.470
Why?

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:35.239
Because the SCP Foundation was immediately
on the case.

00:02:35.239 --> 00:02:40.069
Undercover agents in the US Fish and Wildlife
Service flagged the strange death as anomalous,

00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:44.830
and SCP field personnel arrived to do their
own investigation of the crime scene.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:49.340
There they quickly discovered Andrea’s 3D
glasses - which would eventually be classified

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:52.310
as SCP - 178.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:53.750
An Agent looked over the glasses.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:58.040
There didn’t seem to be anything out of
the ordinary about them, just your regular

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:02.520
cardboard frames with blue and red tinted
film over the eyes.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:06.690
Everything about them seemed normal, so he
tried the glasses on himself.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:11.690
He picked up the open book up off the ground
where Andrea had likely dropped it, and saw

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.200
the Ferris wheel pop up off the page.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.980
Nothing abnormal.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:18.819
Until he turned his head slightly...

00:03:18.819 --> 00:03:25.080
He saw the head of some kind of… thing,
only an inch away from his own, looking over

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.090
his shoulder at the book.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:32.260
Being a trained SCP agent, he maintained his
composure, and looked around the room.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:36.690
As he did he saw that several other creatures
were standing and watching.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:40.910
None of the rest of the recovery team seemed
to notice the creatures, and when the agent

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:43.580
removed SCP - 178, they vanished.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:48.799
It appeared that they had found whatever had
caused Andrea Bradbury’s death.

00:03:48.799 --> 00:03:52.879
The glasses were immediately taken to the
nearest Foundation containment site for further

00:03:52.879 --> 00:03:53.879
testing.

00:03:53.879 --> 00:03:58.380
Seeing these mysterious entities through SCP
- 178 may have answered one question, but

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.599
it raised many others.

00:04:00.599 --> 00:04:01.870
What are these creatures?

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:06.689
Were they real, or merely illusions created
by SCP - 178?

00:04:06.689 --> 00:04:12.990
If they are real, are they somehow summoned
by SCP - 178, or simply revealed by them?

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:17.511
There was already one death that could be
tied to the glasses with some certainty, but

00:04:17.511 --> 00:04:19.320
just how dangerous were they?

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:23.320
The SCP Foundation was about to find out.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:27.550
Foundation scientists devised a series of
experiments, with a test chamber separated

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:32.150
from an adjoining observation chamber by a
panel of reinforced bulletproof glass.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:38.230
A member of D-Class personnel was placed into
the test chamber, along with SCP - 178.

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:42.720
He was instructed to put on the glasses and
report what he saw back to the researchers.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:47.900
The D-Class followed the orders, however when
he did so, he quickly entered a state of extreme

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:49.100
distress.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.690
He threw away the glasses and covered his
eyes, screaming wildly.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:57.320
When ordered to compose himself and explain
what he saw under threat of termination, the

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:02.090
D-Class described a “hideous” creature
standing close to his face, watching.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:06.930
When asked to elaborate, he described it as
having “too many eyes.”

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:11.190
After that, the D-Class refused to put the
glasses back on again, despite direct orders

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.100
and threats from Foundation staff.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:16.120
He was then removed from the test chamber
and observed.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:20.890
Although he experienced two days of mild paranoia,
after thirty total days of observation the

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:24.530
D-Class was found to have no long lasting
psychological effects.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:29.100
Disappointed by the meager results of the
first test, the researchers had at least confirmed

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:35.270
that they did indeed have an anomalous object
in their possession, and pressed on with the

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.270
experiments.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.500
They used the same methodology again on another
D-Class.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:43.520
She was placed into the chamber and instructed
to put on SCP - 178, then describe the entity

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:45.740
she saw in great detail.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:50.800
When she put on the glasses she recoiled in
horror at the monster she saw staring back

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:51.800
at her.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:56.310
She said that the creature was tall and bipedal,
with two additional upper appendages ending

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:58.910
in large conical protrusions.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:03.120
She also described the creature’s head as
being “smooth.”

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:07.720
When asked if the creature exhibited any kind
of aggression or hostility, she said that

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.260
it was completely still.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.630
It was just standing there.

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:16.140
After a few minutes though, the creature seemed
to lose interest, and began staring at the

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:17.140
wall.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:20.760
The researchers were happy to learn more about
the creature’s physicality, but they still

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:24.700
weren’t confident that it wasn’t just
an illusion created by the glasses.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:27.910
They needed to engineer an interaction.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:30.910
For the next experiment, they decided to alter
the particulars.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:35.850
A fractal blue and red image, in a similar
style to the stereoscopic Ferris wheel from

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:39.290
the book Andrea had purchased was fixed to
one wall.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:43.190
Against the opposite wall, they placed a bucket
containing ten standard tennis balls.

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:48.460
This time, the D-Class - a convicted murderer
and arsonist - was told that he was helping

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:51.790
to test a new 3D augmented reality project.

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:56.720
The entities he would see, as far as he knew,
were little more than digital projections.

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:02.470
Though when he actually wore SCP - 178 and
saw them, he commented that whoever designed

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:04.280
them must be crazy.

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:07.750
The researchers instructed the D-Class to
pick up a tennis ball and throw it at one

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:08.910
of the entities.

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:13.400
The second he did so, deep lacerations began
appearing all over his body.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:18.780
The onslaught was brutal and quick, and the
D-Class was dead soon after that.

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:22.880
This confirmed to the researchers that the
creatures did seem to have some level of tangible

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.920
presence, and they could be extremely violent
if provoked.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:32.010
Next, they wished to see if it was possible
to have any kind of interaction with the creatures

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:35.250
without it immediately descending into violence.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:39.520
To test this theory, the researchers brought
a nineteen year old D-Class into the testing

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:44.190
chamber under the same pretence of testing
new 3D technology.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:48.380
Much like the others, she was still horrified
by the appearance of the creatures, but was

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:50.580
calmed down by the researchers.

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:55.300
They asked her to speak to the creatures directly,
without exhibiting any kind of aggression.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:08:00.430
She said, “Hello, weird thing, how are you
today?” in a somewhat bored voice.

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:05.270
And this was all it took to sign her death
warrant - she was immediately slashed to death

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:06.780
by invisible creatures.

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:11.450
The results seemed clear: Any interaction
whatsoever with the creatures while wearing

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:16.470
SCP - 178 was a death sentence, like a slightly
more outgoing Shy Guy.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:21.270
But the researchers would soon find that this
anomaly had even more surprises.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:28.150
For their next test, they brought in two subjects:
One would wear SCP - 178, and dictate to the

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:31.360
other how they should interact with a creature
they could not see.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:35.490
The results of this experiment were bloody,
yet informative.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:39.760
Both subjects were slashed to death when the
unseeing D-Class interacted with one of the

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:42.409
creatures on her companion’s instructions.

00:08:42.409 --> 00:08:46.000
It appeared that anyone with sufficient knowledge
of the creatures who attempts to interact

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:50.120
with them is doomed, even if they can’t
directly see one of them.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:56.630
It was an upsetting realization for the researchers:
SCP - 178 may be much more dangerous than

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:57.760
they initially imagined.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:02.220
And what they’d learn in the next experiment
was even worse.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:07.280
They adopted the same methodology as the last
for the following experiment - two subjects,

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:09.320
one seeing and the other interacting.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:14.590
However, this time, as soon as Subject number
one put on the glasses, they knew that something

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:15.840
was terribly wrong.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:21.360
He began panicking, stating that the entire
chamber was full of the creatures, all standing

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.500
and watching.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:26.030
The researchers undertook these experiments
knowing that they didn’t often turn out

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:30.550
well for the D-Class, so they didn’t seem
too worried about this new development…

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:34.970
that is until the subject stated that they
could see three more of the creatures, and

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.000
they weren’t in the test chamber.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:39.170
They were in the observation room.

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:43.940
In fact, one of them was looking right over
one of the three researchers’ shoulders.

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:47.630
Immediately, the researchers lost composure
and began to panic.

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:51.920
They were used to putting D-Class in danger,
that was part of the job, but they weren’t

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:53.700
prepared for this!

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:58.390
In just moments, the observation room became
a bloodbath as the three researchers who’d

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:03.270
been designing and performing all the experiments
were torn to pieces by creatures they couldn’t

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:04.270
see

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:09.500
SCP - 178 had gone from being one of the more
innocent looking anomalies to one of the most

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.760
mysterious and deadly.

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:15.970
The creatures seemed to be powerful, violent,
and incredibly numerous.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:20.570
The fact that they can only be observed through
178’s stereoscopic lenses and kill anyone

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:24.930
who even attempts to interact with them makes
them almost impossible to understand.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:30.760
It was always a tragedy when the Foundation
lost good researchers, but the work must continue,

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:34.920
and the experiments were soon restarted with
increased safety measures.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:39.290
Of course those didn’t do much good, and
after another disastrous experiment that resulted

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:45.490
in the whole sector getting locked down, all
research into SCP - 178 was placed under increased

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:46.490
scrutiny.

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:50.160
They needed to find some way of observing
the creatures, without the risk of having

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.600
to share space with them.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:56.820
The proposed solution was seeing if the SCP
- 178 glasses were compatible with camera

00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:58.700
technology for remote viewing.

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:03.920
Much like all stereoscopic glasses, they found
that looking through only one lens at a time

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:05.370
was ineffective.

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:10.640
The solution was relatively simple: A dual-lens
camera in a roughly similar configuration

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:11.640
to human eyes.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:15.910
This, however, didn’t give them the comfort,
or the answers they hoped for.

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:20.590
Researchers commented, upon finally seeing
the creatures, that they were even more hideous

00:11:20.590 --> 00:11:22.660
than they’d ever imagined.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:27.001
As they observed a victim interacting with
the creatures via their new camera, they found

00:11:27.001 --> 00:11:31.200
that as soon as the creatures were interacted
with in any way, they would grow three long

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:33.190
claws and attack.

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:36.880
And they were as fast as they were ferocious.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:40.830
From the observations, there were only a few
things that the Foundation now knew about

00:11:40.830 --> 00:11:45.800
them for sure: Their physical appearance,
their violent nature, their enhanced physical

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:49.330
abilities, and the fact they appear to be
pretty much everywhere.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:54.790
And who knows how long they’d been here,
observing us humans while we glided by them,

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:56.510
ignorant to their presence?

00:11:56.510 --> 00:12:01.210
It’s enough to make you think twice before
putting on a pair of 3D glasses again.

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:05.270
But of course, never putting on the glasses
doesn’t mean you’re safe.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:07.860
Just knowing about them puts you in danger.

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:12.810
They could be standing next to you right now,
looking over your shoulder as you watch this

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:14.060
video.

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:20.110
Just remember: If you want to be safe, you
can’t ever let them know you’re aware.

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:26.810
After all, just because you can’t see something,
doesn’t mean it can’t hurt you.

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:33.280
Now go check out “SCP - 049 - The Plague
Doctor Captured” and “SCP - 087 - The

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:36.600
Stairwell” for some other creepy creatures
from SCP Explained!

